      "title": "Quantum computer simulates matter “popping into existence”",
      "description": "Scientists recreated a particle-forming process linked to the extreme physics of the early universe using a 13-ion quantum simulator. The breakthrough suggests quantum computers could eventually help researchers investigate how matter formed and evolved after the Big Bang.",
      "link": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/09/260925005416.htm",
